  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 137 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nBroad upper ridging remains over the southwest states with moderate \njet energy over the northern states. A shortwave moving across the \nnorthern Plains today and through the Great Lakes Sunday drags a \nmodest cold front across Kansas tonight. Southerly flow ahead of it \nbrings dewpoints back into the 50s with light winds and clear skies \nthis evening. With a weak wind field associated with the front \nitself, there is some potential for shallow ground fog formation late\nthis evening into Sunday morning. Most short-term guidance fails to \ngenerate much fog, though progs 24 hours ago for this morning were \nsimilar and there was some shallow ground fog in favored locations. \nAt this point will leave the mention out but it will need to be \nmonitored. Modest north winds behind the front Sunday weaken again \nunder clear skies which presents another potential fog concern. Highs\nSunday and Monday should still be in the 70s in only minor airmass \nchanges.\n\nAnother modest wave to the north pushes another weak front into the \narea Wednesday but warm-air advection ahead of it should supply a \nslightly warmer Tuesday and into the later week periods with above \nnormal temperatures supported by LREF 850 mb temperature means. By \nthis time, the upper flow backs a bit in response to upper energy \nmoves into the west coast. Notable impacts locally from this are not\nanticipated for this forecast period.",
